Beth Friedman  <bjf@wavefront.com> wrote:
><damerell@chiark.greenend.org.uk>,
[the old wishable magic candle thing]
>>Currently when you get an early magic lamp you face a difficult choice;
>>take the (80% chance of a) wish, and maybe never find another, or keep it
>>and risk dying without the magic resistance or reflection it could have
>>brought. If you know you can always wish for a magic candle at the Castle,
>>this dilemma is rendered meaningless.
>That dilemma is all very well, but if you haven't found a magic lamp
>anywhere in the game, it'd be nice to be able to wish for the
>permanent light source.

It's nice but it's not vital; good management of oil lamps, brass
lanterns, potions of oil and spare candles gives light where it's needed.
I don't see it as a problem that players may occasionally be required to
exercise these skills.

>I can't think of any game where I only had
>one magic lamp and I burned it for a wish -- light is just too
>important to me.  

I haven't done this for years, but it's very common in novice play,
suggesting there is a real choice to be made.

>Could the game keep track of whether you'd ever encountered a magic
>lamp, and only allow you to wish a magic candle if you hadn't?

That's certainly feasible, but ugly and lacks consistency.

>Or a radical suggestion -- how about instead of a guaranteed wand of
>wishing at the castle, there are between 1 and 5 blessed magic lamps?
>That would make the issue moot and give slightly fewer wishes.

This has exactly the same problem; if I found an early magic lamp I'd burn
it, assured of permanent light at the castle.

>I always thought the castle wand of wishing made the game a bit too
>unbalanced.

In general I think WoW give too many wishes, especially now that there is
more flexibility in the ascension kit. Fewer wishes per wand would both
make an early WoW less of a game-breaker, and potentially leave players
with unresolved equipment problems after the Castle - at the same time,
you'd always be able to get magic resistance and reflection if you didn't
have them already, as long as a wand offered a mere 2 wishes.
